    {
      "id": "XCHaTOdAWVAiSSMVcTNxP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1264.7893067258942,
      "y": -4977.002980081689,
      "width": 108.89793171595808,
      "height": 131.7957572178862,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 332037859,
      "version": 326,
      "versionNonce": 1577825805,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "OsOm8Mj5drK4y83mZ0S6h",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1778037692799,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " Solo Tool (just for you)\n\n  Pros\n  - Ship in days, not weeks\n  - No auth, no user management, no roles\n  - Hardcode your own constraints as defaults — less UI needed\n  - No need to handle edge cases other people would hit\n  - Can use your own API keys / credentials directly\n  - Easier to iterate — just change the code and re-run\n\n  Cons\n  - Not shareable — if a teammate wants to use it, they can't without your help\n  - No audit trail of who searched what\n  - If you leave or the machine breaks, it's gone\n\n  ---\n  Team Tool\n\n  Pros\n  - Everyone on the team can search independently\n  - Can save and share search results / shortlists between members\n  - Can collect votes or comments on candidate locations\n  - More durable — hosted somewhere, not tied to your laptop\n\n  Cons\n  - Needs login / auth (even just a shared password)\n  - Needs a database to store searches and results\n  - Needs deployment and hosting (more DevOps work)\n  - Takes 2–4x longer to build the first version\n  - More complex to maintain\n\n  ---\n  My suggestion\n\n  Start as a solo tool, design for team later.\n\n  Build v1 for yourself with a clean separation between \"my hardcoded config\" and \"the\n  core logic.\" When you're ready to share, the core logic is already solid and you just\n   wrap it with auth + a hosted UI. This is the standard \"dogfood it yourself first\"\n  approach — you'll also discover what constraints actually matter before exposing it\n  to teammates.",
      "fontSize": 2.5716245310807087,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " Solo Tool (just for you)\n\n  Pros\n  - Ship in days, not weeks\n  - No auth, no user management, no roles\n  - Hardcode your own constraints as defaults — less UI needed\n  - No need to handle edge cases other people would hit\n  - Can use your own API keys / credentials directly\n  - Easier to iterate — just change the code and re-run\n\n  Cons\n  - Not shareable — if a teammate wants to use it, they can't without your help\n  - No audit trail of who searched what\n  - If you leave or the machine breaks, it's gone\n\n  ---\n  Team Tool\n\n  Pros\n  - Everyone on the team can search independently\n  - Can save and share search results / shortlists between members\n  - Can collect votes or comments on candidate locations\n  - More durable — hosted somewhere, not tied to your laptop\n\n  Cons\n  - Needs login / auth (even just a shared password)\n  - Needs a database to store searches and results\n  - Needs deployment and hosting (more DevOps work)\n  - Takes 2–4x longer to build the first version\n  - More complex to maintain\n\n  ---\n  My suggestion\n\n  Start as a solo tool, design for team later.\n\n  Build v1 for yourself with a clean separation between \"my hardcoded config\" and \"the\n  core logic.\" When you're ready to share, the core logic is already solid and you just\n   wrap it with auth + a hosted UI. This is the standard \"dogfood it yourself first\"\n  approach — you'll also discover what constraints actually matter before exposing it\n  to teammates.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
