      "updated": 1778046788757,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is ToS (Terms of Service)?\n\n  It's a legal agreement between you and the website. When you use a site, you\n  implicitly agree to their rules. For scraping, the key question is: \"Does this site\n  allow automated access / data collection?\"\n\n  Most Korean real estate sites say no in their ToS — but the practical risk varies a\n  lot.\n\n  ---\n  What to Look For in a ToS\n\n  When you read a ToS, search for these keywords:\n\n  ┌───────────────────┬─────────────────────┬────────────────────────┐\n  │    Korean term    │   English meaning   │ Red flag if it says... │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 자동화된 접근     │ Automated access    │ \"금지\" (prohibited)    │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 크롤링 / 스크래핑 │ Crawling / scraping │ \"허용하지 않습니다\"    │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 수집              │ Data collection     │ \"무단 수집 금지\"       │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ robots.txt        │ Bot access rules    │ Disallow: /            │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 상업적 이용       │ Commercial use      │ \"금지\"                 │\n  └───────────────────┴─────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n\n  ---\n  How to Review Each Site\n\n  Step 1 — Find the ToS page\n\n  ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐\n  │     Site     │          Where to look           │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Naver 부동산 │ land.naver.com → 하단 \"이용약관\" │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 직방         │ zigbang.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"    │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 다방         │ dabang.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"     │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 피터팬       │ peterpanz.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"  │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 호갱노노     │ hogangnono.com → 하단 \"이용약관\" │\n  └──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘\n\n  Step 2 — Check robots.txt\n\n  This is the most important technical signal. Every site has a file at /robots.txt\n  that tells bots what they can and can't access.\n\n  Go to these URLs directly in your browser:\n  https://land.naver.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.zigbang.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.dabang.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.peterpanz.com/robots.txt\n  https://hogangnono.com/robots.txt\n\n  Look for:\n  # Good — specific pages blocked, most allowed\n  Disallow: /admin/\n\n  # Bad — everything blocked\n  Disallow: /\n\n  # Neutral — only certain bots blocked\n  User-agent: Googlebot\n  Allow: /\n  User-agent: *\n  Disallow: /\n\n  ---\n  Risk Spectrum (Practical View)\n\n  ┌──────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Risk    │               Situation               │        What happens         │\n  │  level   │                                       │                             │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Low      │ Personal use, low frequency,          │ Almost never enforced       │\n  │          │ robots.txt allows it                  │                             │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Medium   │ Personal use, robots.txt disallows it │ IP block, no legal action   │\n  │          │                                       │ typically                   │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ High     │ Commercial product, selling data,     │ Legal letter, lawsuit       │\n  │          │ high volume                           │ possible                    │\n  └──────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘",
      "fontSize": 2.3011764914936115,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is ToS (Terms of Service)?\n\n  It's a legal agreement between you and the website. When you use a site, you\n  implicitly agree to their rules. For scraping, the key question is: \"Does this site\n  allow automated access / data collection?\"\n\n  Most Korean real estate sites say no in their ToS — but the practical risk varies a\n  lot.\n\n  ---\n  What to Look For in a ToS\n\n  When you read a ToS, search for these keywords:\n\n  ┌───────────────────┬─────────────────────┬────────────────────────┐\n  │    Korean term    │   English meaning   │ Red flag if it says... │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 자동화된 접근     │ Automated access    │ \"금지\" (prohibited)    │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 크롤링 / 스크래핑 │ Crawling / scraping │ \"허용하지 않습니다\"    │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 수집              │ Data collection     │ \"무단 수집 금지\"       │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ robots.txt        │ Bot access rules    │ Disallow: /            │\n  ├───────────────────┼─────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\n  │ 상업적 이용       │ Commercial use      │ \"금지\"                 │\n  └───────────────────┴─────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n\n  ---\n  How to Review Each Site\n\n  Step 1 — Find the ToS page\n\n  ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐\n  │     Site     │          Where to look           │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Naver 부동산 │ land.naver.com → 하단 \"이용약관\" │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 직방         │ zigbang.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"    │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 다방         │ dabang.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"     │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 피터팬       │ peterpanz.com → 하단 \"이용약관\"  │\n  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ 호갱노노     │ hogangnono.com → 하단 \"이용약관\" │\n  └──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘\n\n  Step 2 — Check robots.txt\n\n  This is the most important technical signal. Every site has a file at /robots.txt\n  that tells bots what they can and can't access.\n\n  Go to these URLs directly in your browser:\n  https://land.naver.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.zigbang.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.dabang.com/robots.txt\n  https://www.peterpanz.com/robots.txt\n  https://hogangnono.com/robots.txt\n\n  Look for:\n  # Good — specific pages blocked, most allowed\n  Disallow: /admin/\n\n  # Bad — everything blocked\n  Disallow: /\n\n  # Neutral — only certain bots blocked\n  User-agent: Googlebot\n  Allow: /\n  User-agent: *\n  Disallow: /\n\n  ---\n  Risk Spectrum (Practical View)\n\n  ┌──────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Risk    │               Situation               │        What happens         │\n  │  level   │                                       │                             │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Low      │ Personal use, low frequency,          │ Almost never enforced       │\n  │          │ robots.txt allows it                  │                             │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Medium   │ Personal use, robots.txt disallows it │ IP block, no legal action   │\n  │          │                                       │ typically                   │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\n  │ High     │ Commercial product, selling data,     │ Legal letter, lawsuit       │\n  │          │ high volume                           │ possible                    │\n  └──────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
